<title>BELGIUM: EU raps Argentina for limiting hide exports.</title>
<headline>EU raps Argentina for limiting hide exports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>In one of the European Union's more unusual trade complaints, its executive Commission has complained to Argentina for not exporting enough of a product.</p>
<p>In a statement, the Commission said it was challenging Argentina &quot;for severely limiting the export of cow hide to the EU, thereby choking off an essential supply of raw material for European producers&quot;.</p>
<p>The Commission said Argentina operated a tacit export ban on raw cow hide by means of a 15 percent export tax and also by imposing a three percent duty on imports of finished leather goods.</p>
<p>&quot;The combined effect of export restrictions on raw materials -- with high quality Argentine bovine hides being reserved for Argentine use only -- and import measures on unfinished leather have allowed the Argentinian tanning industry to undercut EU tanners' prices ... undermining the latter's competitive position,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The complaint was raised by a European tanning association and the Commission has begun an investigation, it added.</p>
